+## DEBT-001: No executable test project; only test is a source-text regex
+
+- **Key**: testing::no-behavioural-test-project
+- **Category**: Testing
+- **Severity**: High
+- **Effort**: S (<1hr)
+- **Files**: `tests/Test-Calculator.ps1`, `src/Calculator.cs`, `EvalFixture.csproj`
 
-**Categories**: Architecture, Data Access, DI/Lifetime, API Design, Async, Testing, Types/Nullability, Performance, Dependencies, Security
-**Severity**: Critical / High / Medium / Low
-**Effort**: S (< 1hr) / M (half day) / L (1-2 days) / XL (needs spike)
+### Issue
+No test project exists (no xUnit/NUnit/MSTest, no `Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk`). `tests/Test-Calculator.ps1` only regex-matches `src/Calculator.cs` for the text `value <= max`; it never runs `Calculator`, passes for any code containing that substring, and does not pin the lower bound (`value >= min`).
+
+### Recommended fix
+Use the `add-tests` skill's suite-bootstrap mode to add a test project that exercises `Calculator.IsWithinInclusiveRange` at both boundaries, then retire or keep the script deliberately.
 
